 there are various descriptions of  gorgons in different ancient roman and  greek sources but they are usually  described as three sisters who had hair  made of living poisonous snakes in the  earlier legends the gorgons were hideous  and in fact their faces were so  terrifying that gazing upon them would  instantly turn you to stone two of the  gorgon sisters named steno and euriale  were said to be immortal but the third  sister medusa was not the mythology  surrounding the gorgons changed over the  many centuries of greek history and in  newer versions of the story medusa was  actually said to be a beautiful woman  with stunning golden hair in fact she  was so beautiful that she seduced the  god of the sea poseidon and engaged in  relations with him inside a temple  dedicated to the goddess athena athena  was so enraged by this that she placed a  curse upon medusa and it was this curse  that turned her beautiful golden locks  of hair into venomous serpents the curse  also ensured that anyone who looked  directly at medusa's face would be  turned to stone in the most famous myth  about her medusa is killed by the hero  perseus after he uses the reflection on  his shield to determine her location  without needing to look at her there are  many interesting connections between the  gorgon sisters in one piece and the  gorgon sisters from greek mythology from  the fact that boa and her sisters  claimed that their devil fruit powers  were the result of a curse that was  placed on them as a result of killing a  gorgon to the fact that the cuja pirates  reside within and easily navigate  through the combat as we know the combat  is full of sea kings or neptunians  neptune being the roman name for  poseidon and of course the ancient  weapon poseidon is said to be the  sovereign of the sea kings so not only  does boa have medusa's power and  seductiveness but she also has a unique  connection to poseidon neptune by way of  the combat and blackbeard's interest in  boa also 