 incident  when he was only 2 years old many have  speculated that blackbeard wants revenge  for the death of his father and for the  fact that he had to live his entire life  as an orphan him naming his ship the  saber of zebek is a blatant clue that  blackbeard intends to finish what zebek  started 40 years earlier he plans to  carry out zebec's master plan of  overthrowing the world government and  becoming the king of the world if we  accept that blackbeard was in part  inspired by hades and cerberus from  greek mythology then who would be the  inspiration for zebic a good place to  start is the father of cerberus typhon  who is a monster god and the father of  all the monsters he was a fire breeding  chimera even more terrifying than  cerberus himself  gaia and tartarus created typhon in  order to defeat zeus and the olympian  gods after they overthrew gaia's  children the titans typhon was able to  easily overpower all the olympian gods  except for zeus zeus fought typhon but  he lost the first battle and typhon tore  off his tendons in the process as an  injured zeus went into hiding on mount  olympus hermes was able to use his speed  to get zeus his tendons back eventually  zeus was able to defeat typhon by  hurling hundreds of lightning bolts at  him and then he placed an entire  mountain on top of him in order to stop  him from escaping this is extremely  interesting to me because in greek  mythology you have the ancient gods the  titans being overthrown by the new  olympian gods during the divine war  known as the titanomachi kind of like  the war between the ancient kingdom and  the alliance that became the world  government in one piece then you have  typhon coming in to try to overthrow the  olympian gods kind of like zebek  declared war on the world government and  tried to overthrow them but ultimately  failed however  typhon did leave a legacy behind he is  the father of all the monsters just like  the remnants of zevek's crew the rox  pirates all b